     \item \textbf{Creeping behavior.} Allowing vehicles to partially advance during lane-change waits would improve realism and throughput prediction, particularly at high-demand weaving sections.
 
+    \item \textbf{Transfer to a second contended-space domain.} The resource protocol is stated independently of vehicles, but only one domain is reported here. Applying it to another discrete-space system in which occupancy is exclusive and waiting is the congestion mechanism, such as block-signalled rail or automated warehouse aisles, would test whether the analytical tractability shown in Section~\ref{sec:analytical} is a property of the protocol or of the traffic case.
+
     \item \textbf{Advanced AV coordination.} The decoupled architecture enables integration of cooperative AV behaviors (platoon formation, coordinated lane changes, V2V communication) as controller modules, without modifying the underlying movement engine.
